--- C00.md ---

> ## Step-by-Step
  
  1. Pin down the opaque target as a precise quantity. Take the informal question — why did it decide this, how much di
d this datum matter, how confident should it be — and commit to a formal definition of responsibility or uncertainty ra
ther than leaving it implicit. A definition you cannot defend as the 'real' quantity (no soundness argument, no axiomat
ic grounding) is the first thing reviewers attack, so make the definition itself a load-bearing claim, not a notational
 convenience.
  2. Map the quantity onto an existing well-understood object and its solver. Recognize the target as an instance of co
unterfactual optimization, subset selection, expectation estimation, basis decomposition, or influence/Shapley allocati
on so that mature machinery and guarantees apply. Choose the object whose native correctness criterion already coincide
s with what 'faithful' means for your quantity, rather than the one that is merely most familiar.
  3. Fix the unit of analysis and the faithfulness constraint before computing anything. Decide whether the atoms are r
aw inputs, grouped regions, native architectural components, or a learned sparse basis, and impose the constraint that 
