ranking or value it approximates; a fast approximation that silently changes the quantity is no better than the heurist
ic it replaces.
  5. Certify fidelity causally or by proof, not by plausibility. Validate that perturbing or ablating the identified ob
ject actually shifts model behavior in the predicted direction, or prove the estimator is unbiased, optimal, or sound u
nder stated conditions. Correlational evidence, eyeballed heatmaps, or 'looks reasonable' without a confound-controllin
