> ## Step-by-Step
  
  1. Identify which supervision component the native formulation silently assumes but cannot obtain — optimal demonstra
tions, dense reward labels, or ground-truth action annotations — and reframe the bottleneck as a missing-supervision pr
oblem rather than an architecture or loss-function problem. The whole tactic hinges on locating the absent ingredient p
recisely, because the recast will be built around fabricating exactly that ingredient.
  2. Choose a target object class whose mature solvers do NOT need the missing component: supervised likelihood / distr
ibution matching, autoregressive sequence prediction, or an invertible generative prior. Prefer an object whose machine
ry is self-contained and battle-tested in adjacent fields, so the contribution is the reframing plus the substitution, 
not the invention of a new solver.
  3. Manufacture the missing supervision from data that already exists: retrospectively relabel each achieved outcome a
s its own optimal target, derive a self-supervised proxy signal (future reachability, inverse dynamics, latent mode), o
r pre-train a frozen generative prior/world model on cheap unlabeled or task-agnostic interaction. Make the substituted
 signal load-bearing and faithful — avoid exact-algebraic equivalences that hold only under brittle assumptions, since 
a substitution that is only approximately valid forfeits the guarantees the recast was meant to import.
  4. Make the recast tractable by compressing the continuous, high-dimensional native space into the object's natural r
epresentation — tokenize observations/actions into a discrete vocabulary, quantize the latent goal space into a prototy
pe set — and verify the compression preserves the modes and diversity the native problem requires. Collapse to a single
 behavioral mode (unimodal imitation) is the diagnostic that the compression destroyed what the recast needed to captur
e.
  5. Demonstrate that the recast unlocks a capability the native formulation lacked, at a scale that pre-empts the 'ana
lysis-only' and 'toy-only' critiques: post a clear empirical win over native-formulation baselines on non-trivial bench
marks, ablate that the gain comes from the manufactured-supervision move rather than incidental architecture, and expla
in any boundary behavior rather than leaving an unexplained degradation that undercuts the generalization claim.
  
