--- C14.md ---
> ## Step-by-Step
  
  1. Localize the cost to one specific operator and write down explicitly the property it must preserve. Pin the bottle
neck to a single object — the dense all-pairs interaction, an iterated propagation, a joint tensor product — and name t
he property whose loss would break the model: expressive class, receptive-field reach, retrieval capacity, or ordering 
sensitivity. Skipping this and treating the swap as self-evidently cheaper leaves no yardstick for fidelity and invites
 the 'rigorous but already believed' dismissal.
  2. Choose a surrogate whose cheapness comes from an algebraic or structural lever, not from discarding inputs. Pick a
 primitive — kernel/random-feature factorization, convolution, state-space scan, structured factored matrix, hierarchic
al or sparse routing — whose lower cost follows from associativity, factorization, or compression so that no element is
 dropped from the interaction. Surrogates that buy speed by pruning, downsampling, or windowing away interactions tend 
to trade off the very property named in step 1.
  3. Prove the surrogate preserves that property, surfacing the hidden invariant the fast computation secretly depends 
on. Either derive an approximation/equivalence bound or exhibit an exact algebraic identity, and explicitly identify an
d enforce the structural precondition the rewrite needs — positivity of the kernel, a low-rank-plus-normal decompositio
n, an order-preserving parameterization. A fidelity proof that never connects to a consequence, or a swap that silently
 violates the invariant, is the most common fatal gap.
  4. Demonstrate that the substitution itself is the causal driver by controlling every confound. Hold fixed positional
 encodings, parameter count, added multi-scale or capacity features, and the training recipe so the measured gain canno
t be attributed to anything but the operator swap, and benchmark not only against the expensive original but against th
e existing family of cheaper surrogates. Omitting the surrogate-family baselines makes the work read as a redundant rep
arameterization, and uncontrolled confounds make the headline conclusion unattributable.
  5. Stress-test in the exact regime the substitution targets and state the consequence it unlocks. Evaluate at the sca
le or input length where the original operator fails — very long sequences, very large element sets, higher representat
ional orders — and articulate what the swap delivers beyond efficiency: a previously infeasible task, a resolved effici
ency-versus-quality tradeoff, or imported theory that reframes the operator. Small-scale-only validation, or a swap wit
h no demonstrated downstream consequence, leaves the core promise untested.
  
  ## Differentiation within parent
--- C30.md ---
> ## Step-by-Step
  
  1. Name the exact second-order quantity that governs the outcome you care about — not 'curvature is expensive' but th
e specific spectral object: the smallest eigenvalue that throttles the step size, the outlier eigenvalues that create s
purious minima, the limiting kernel's positive-definiteness, or the dimension of the conserved-quantity space. Tie the 
bottleneck (slow convergence, trapped optimization, infeasible attribution) to this one quantity. Attempts that merely 
observe 'second-order methods are costly' and reach for a generic proxy without isolating which spectral quantity is lo
ad-bearing will read as incremental.
  2. Pick the substitution direction. Either (a) replace the object with a structurally cheaper surrogate that keeps th
e load-bearing spectral content, or (b) reparameterize/lift the variable so the spectrum itself is reshaped in your fav
or. The surrogate or reparameterization must exploit a structural property latent in *this* problem — low-rank update i
ncrements, a factorized parameterization, composability across operator types, an invariant subspace — rather than impo
rting an off-the-shelf approximation that happens to be cheap.
  3. Prove that the substitute preserves the essential spectral property for your actual structure. Establish positive-
definiteness of the *composite* matrix (e.g. when operator-constrained terms mix direct and transformed evaluations), d
erive the saddle-escape or rank-threshold result, or show the cheap and expensive criteria are *exactly* equivalent. Do
 not assume a positive-definiteness or no-spurious-minima result from a prior, simpler setting carries over by analogy 
— the composite/operator-mixed object usually breaks the inherited proof and the gap must be closed independently.
  4. Convert the spectral guarantee into the end-quantity the field rewards: a finite, computable threshold (lifting de
gree, factorization rank), a convergence rate decoupled from the condition number, a generalization or attribution boun
d, or a completeness claim that no further invariants exist. The condition under which the guarantee binds must be veri
fiable and non-vacuous; a bound resting on an unproven ansatz, or one that degrades under the curse of dimensionality o
r unestimable distributional structure, undermines the whole chain.
  5. Validate that the substitution moves the needle against the strongest available baseline — the cheap surrogate mat
ches the exact second-order method's quality, or the reshaped landscape delivers the claimed escape/convergence empiric
ally. A correct theorem proven only in a contrived regime (width-1 layers, a single response-function form, infinite wi
dth with no finite-width discussion) or shipped without strong baselines reads as an artifact of the assumptions rather
 than a general advance.
  
  ## Differentiation within parent
--- C02.md ---
> ## Step-by-Step
  
  1. Name the exact confound and the true property it masks. Write down the single manipulable artifact you believe is 
inflating the current measurement — a memorized test set, a surface-style cue, the generating source's capability, a si
ngle-modality shortcut, a nonlinear scoring function, or task-format exposure — and state precisely which property it i
s being mistaken for. A diffuse 'this benchmark is flawed' framing is insufficient; instruments whose target confound i
s never pinned to one variable are turned away as vague.
  2. Construct controlled instances that block or independently vary that one confound while holding everything else fi
xed. Use synthetic generation from a formal spec, typed-slot templates with consistency constraints, per-cue suppressio
n, provenance/timestamp gating, realism stratification, or matched same-source pairs with injected defects — whatever i
solates the chosen axis. Keep all other axes constant so any measured difference is attributable to the confound alone;
 uncontrolled co-variation between surface change and structural change is the most common reason the isolation claim f
ails.
  3. Supply ground truth that is independent of the system under evaluation. Verifiability must come from how the insta
nce was constructed — a known derivation path, a planted failure region, a mechanistic pass/fail criterion, an exchange
ability-based null distribution — never from the evaluand's own consensus or a self-asserted, contested definition. Des
igns whose oracle is the very population being judged, or that hardcode the definition they claim to test, are rejected
 for circularity.
  4. Report the divergence between apparent and de-confounded performance as the headline result, and ensure it reveals
 something not knowable in advance. The contribution is the gap itself — a discontinuity that disappears, a score that 
drops sharply, a partition that splits cleanly — not a restatement of a limitation the field already accepted. An instr
ument that merely re-confirms a documented shortcut, surfacing no previously unmeasurable failure, reads as confirmator
y and is declined.
  5. Bound the claim to exactly what the instances probe and demonstrate the isolated signal survives outside the contr
olled regime. Show transfer from synthetic to realistic conditions, or explicitly scope the conclusion to the task stru
cture actually tested. A narrow single-task or small-N instrument carrying broad capability claims invites a scope-mism
atch rejection, and a synthetic-only result with no real-world corroboration invites an ecological-validity rejection.
  
  ## Differentiation within parent


