C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C30.md:16:## Differentiation within parent
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C30.md:20:## When to pick this one
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C30.md:22:Choose this instantiation when your bottleneck lives in the second-order structure of the training dynamics — the Hessian/NTK/Fisher spectrum, ill-conditioning, spurious-minima or saddle geometry, or curvature-based scoring — rather than in a forward-pass operator's runtime or a representation's expressive capacity. The tell is that the quantity you need to control is a spectral property of how learning proceeds, not of what the network computes on a single input.
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C30.md:24:## Tactical failure mode
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C30.md:26:The dominant failure is substituting curvature for a recognized cheaper proxy — a fixed Hessian approximation, an incrementally-maintained sketch, a continuous-ODE reformulation, or a standard NTK-style preconditioner — and applying it to a new but narrow setting, so the work reads as an incremental re-skin of a known technique rather than a new spectral insight. A second, deeper failure is letting the spectral-preservation claim rest on an unproven ansatz or on a positive-definiteness result borrowed from a simpler regime that does not actually transfer to the composite/operator-mixed object; when the linchpin assumption is only empirically motivated, every downstream theorem collapses with it. A related shortcut is proving the curvature-decoupling or acceleration guarantee only in a contrived regime — width-1 layers, a single response-function form, infinite width with no finite-width bridge — which makes the result an artifact of the assumption. The recurring self-check: have I isolated *which* spectral quantity my substitute uniquely preserves, proven that preservation for *my* structure rather than by analogy, and shown the guarantee binds outside a toy regime against a strong baseline? If the surrogate is general but the proof is borrowed, or the proof is rigorous but the regime is contrived, the contribution will not clear the bar.
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C30.md:28:## Examples
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C30.md:29:### Oral lessons
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C30.md:34:- When practitioners declare a factored curvature approximation inapplicable to a heterogeneous architecture, the highest-yield move is often composing already-existing per-operator-type extensions, not inventing a new approximation.
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C30.md:37:### Reject lessons
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C12.md:4:## Tactical pattern
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C12.md:8:## Step-by-Step
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C12.md:16:## Differentiation within parent
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C12.md:20:## When to pick this one
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C12.md:22:Pick this when the bottleneck lives in a staged network's structural plumbing — where trainable parameters sit, how stages connect, or what operator aggregates per stage — and you can name a classical-theorem-grounded or bijectively-equivalent surrogate that fits that exact slot while flipping a cost or expressivity property. Choose a scoring-function decomposition (14) instead if the bottleneck is inside a single interaction term, or an estimator reparameterization (30) if it is in the optimization landscape rather than the forward graph.
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C12.md:24:## Tactical failure mode
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C12.md:28:## Examples
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C12.md:29:### Oral lessons
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C12.md:37:### Reject lessons
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C21.md:4:## Tactical pattern
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C21.md:6:This cluster recasts reinforcement-learning and sequential-control problems — which natively require reward signals, action labels, or expert demonstrations — as supervised or generative-sequence-modeling problems by manufacturing the absent supervision from interaction data that already exists. The concrete moves are: retrospectively relabel each collected trajectory's target to the outcome it actually achieved (turning suboptimal traces into optimal demonstrations for pure distribution matching); discretize continuous observations or actions into a token vocabulary and forecast them autoregressively as a sequence; and pre-train a frozen generative world model or behavioral prior on cheap unlabeled/task-agnostic interaction, then route downstream control through it. When labels are entirely absent, the missing reward/action component is itself replaced by a self-supervised proxy — future reachability, multi-step inverse dynamics, latent behavioral modes, or a low-capacity causal bottleneck that recovers a latent action space from consecutive states. The payoff is that mature supervised/generative machinery (transformers, normalizing flows, VQ encoders, maximum-likelihood estimation) applies directly, eliminating online optimization, reward design, or the need for gold-standard demonstrations.
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C21.md:8:## Step-by-Step
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C21.md:16:## Differentiation within parent
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C21.md:20:## When to pick this one
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C21.md:22:Pick this instantiation when the sequential-decision problem is blocked specifically by absent supervision — no reward signal, no action annotations, or no optimal demonstrations — yet abundant unlabeled or task-agnostic interaction data is available to manufacture targets from. If instead the blocker is competitive or allocation structure (favoring a game/equilibrium recast) or an opaque scoring computation that needs interpretable predictors, a different sibling fits better.
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C21.md:24:## Tactical failure mode
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C21.md:26:Papers attempting this recast fail when the reframe does not actually unlock a capability the native formulation lacked at a credible scale. One recurring shape: the recast is deployed as a descriptive evaluation or analysis lens — for instance relabeling objectives post-hoc to score collected data — but the accompanying method posts no clear empirical win, so reviewers read it as a benchmark study rather than a contribution. A second shape: the substitution of the missing component rests on a brittle exact assumption, such as the target objective being an exact algebraic combination of source objectives, whose solving machinery does not scale and whose formal guarantees evaporate the moment the assumption holds only approximately. A third shape: the recast is validated only on toy environments and an unexplained boundary behavior — performance degrading past a certain horizon or context length — directly undercuts the generalization claim the reframe was supposed to deliver. Self-check: can you show the manufactured-supervision object beating native-formulation baselines on a non-trivial benchmark, with the gain attributed to the recast and any boundary behavior explained, rather than offering observations or toy-scale wins?
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C21.md:28:## Examples
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C21.md:29:### Oral lessons
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C21.md:37:### Reject lessons
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C21.md:38:- A reframe used only as an evaluation or analysis lens, without a method that posts a clear win, reads as a descriptive benchmark and falls below the novelty bar even when the framing is reusable.
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C09.md:4:## Tactical pattern
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C09.md:8:## Step-by-Step
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C09.md:16:## Differentiation within parent
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C09.md:20:## When to pick this one
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C09.md:22:Pick this when the bottleneck is a per-element sensitivity, disclosure, or verification cost that scales with ambient dimension, runtime, or solution-set size, and there is (or can be built) a compact object the computation routes through whose per-element influence is provably bounded. The tell is a formal privacy/confidentiality/adaptive-adversary constraint where the cost is an artifact of attaching the mechanism to the raw input or final output rather than to that intermediate.
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C09.md:24:## Tactical failure mode
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C09.md:28:## Examples
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C09.md:29:### Oral lessons
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C09.md:32:- When efficient non-private algorithms already route through compact, sparse, bounded-range intermediates, privatize those intermediates directly instead of designing new approximation algorithms from scratch.
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C09.md:37:### Reject lessons
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C09.md:40:- Porting an aggregation rule across settings collapses when its correctness rests on an assumption that may not hold and the key theorem appeal is not rigorously nailed down.
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C27.md:4:## Tactical pattern
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C27.md:8:## Step-by-Step
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C27.md:16:## Differentiation within parent
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C27.md:20:## When to pick this one
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C27.md:22:Pick this instantiation when the problem can be endowed with multiple interacting decision-makers whose competing or cooperating incentives — and a stable fixed point among them — naturally express the quantity you want to compute, and when mature equilibrium-solving machinery (regret minimization, best response, complexity reductions) already exists to exploit.
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C27.md:24:## Tactical failure mode
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C27.md:28:## Examples
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C27.md:29:### Oral lessons
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C27.md:37:### Reject lessons
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C27.md:42:- Extending bounds to a richer setting (noise, multiple groups) collapses when the success criterion stays undefined and the bounds are too loose to inform any real decision.
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C00.md:4:## Tactical pattern
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C00.md:6:This cluster recasts an opaque transparency question about an already-trained model or dataset — which feature/datum/internal component is responsible, how uncertain a prediction is, what a hidden representation encodes — as a concrete measurement over a well-studied object: a manifold-constrained counterfactual optimization, a submodular subset selection, an expectation/estimator over marginal statistics, an additive decomposition into a (often sparse) basis, or an influence/Shapley score accumulated along the optimization trajectory. The decisive move is choosing the right unit of analysis and the right faithfulness constraint so the resulting scores reflect the model's actual computation rather than an off-distribution or post-hoc artifact — e.g., searching counterfactuals only on the learned data manifold, decomposing into monosemantic sparse directions before causal tracing, or embedding the explanatory predictors as the primary decision representation. Tractability is then bought with a single compression trick (random projection, greedy submodular search, fixed-size accumulator vectors, closed-form per-step expansion). Fidelity is finally certified either by a causal intervention that flips model behavior when the identified object is perturbed, or by a soundness/optimality proof, rather than by the visual plausibility of the produced explanation.
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C00.md:8:## Step-by-Step
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C00.md:16:## Differentiation within parent
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C00.md:20:## When to pick this one
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C00.md:22:Pick this instantiation when the problem is to explain, attribute, or quantify confidence about a single already-trained model or fixed dataset and you need a faithful per-unit responsibility or uncertainty score — not when the structure is competitive/multi-party (which favors an equilibrium reframe) or generative across successive populations. The tell is a fixed artifact whose internal behavior you must measure, plus an existing measurement object (counterfactual, subset selection, decomposition, influence/Shapley, causal mediation) you can validate by perturbing the model itself.
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C00.md:24:## Tactical failure mode
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C00.md:28:## Examples
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C00.md:29:### Oral lessons
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C00.md:30:- Embedding the explanatory quantities as the primary basis of the model's decision — rather than fitting them as a separate post-hoc proxy — makes an explanation sound by construction, even when it introduces a circular dependency you must resolve with lagged targets.
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C00.md:34:- Pairing a discovered internal structure with a causal intervention that flips behavior when it is perturbed converts correlational interpretability into causal evidence reviewers trust.
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C00.md:35:- When the quantity you want is provably simpler than the model that produces it, estimate it directly from available marginal statistics and skip the model-fitting detour entirely.
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C00.md:37:### Reject lessons
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C14.md:4:## Tactical pattern
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C14.md:8:## Step-by-Step
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C14.md:16:## Differentiation within parent
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C14.md:20:## When to pick this one
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C14.md:22:Pick this instantiation when the bottleneck is concretely the dense pairwise-interaction (all-pairs / softmax-attention) operator over N elements and you can name a cheaper primitive whose preserved property — expressivity class, receptive field, or retrieval capacity — you can prove or exactly equate. Do not pick it when the operator's cost is acceptable but its mechanism is misunderstood (a re-explanation move) or when the expense lives in estimation/optimization rather than the forward interaction.
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C14.md:24:## Tactical failure mode
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C14.md:26:Papers in this cluster fail when the surrogate is offered as a cheaper-but-equivalent reparameterization with no load-bearing consequence: the preservation argument is absent, trivially true ('already believed by the field'), or proven yet never connected to a capability the original operator lacked. A second recurring shape is the unattributable gain — the operator swap co-varies with a confound (positional encoding, added parameters, multi-scale features, different pre-training data) and no controlled ablation isolates the substitution as the cause. A third is baseline myopia: comparing only against the expensive original while ignoring the established family of cheaper surrogates, so the contribution reads as a redundant re-derivation. These frequently combine with empirical thinness — validation only at small scale or short sequences, never stress-tested in the long-context or large-element regime the substitution is meant to rescue. A candidate author should self-check: have I proven the preserved property actually matters, ruled out every confound, beaten the existing surrogate family, and tested at the regime where the original operator breaks?
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C14.md:28:## Examples
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C14.md:29:### Oral lessons
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C14.md:30:- When two failure modes are conventionally patched separately, showing they share a single root cause lets one operator substitution resolve both at once — a far stronger contribution than two independent fixes.
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C14.md:32:- When an expressive operator resists efficient computation because of a localized numerical pathology, decompose it so the pathology sits in a small exactly-handled correction term and the remainder admits the fast algorithm.
C:\Users\Raymond\Documents\Codex\2026-08-26\https-github-com-microsoft-researchstudio-git\work\ResearchStudio\ResearchStudio-Idea\skills\idea_spark\references\ideation-sub-patterns\C14.md:37:### Reject lessons

