+  "core_mechanism_steps": "1. Freeze the public artifacts and inference contract. Use the exact official Fast-WAM released checkpoint selected for the run manifest as checkpoint_FW, set mode_FW=idm, sigma_shift_FW=1.0, and inference_path_FW=infer_action with the README's current no-default-VAE-decoding behavior; do not substitute first_frame because it removes the future branch. Set b_lo to the matched QuantWAMs W4A4-dominant numerical weight/activation setting, keep the action/video coupling unchanged, and output a versioned configuration manifest with the checkpoint filename, repository revision, mode, sigma shift, inference path, and low-bit kernels. The minimal validation uses Fast-WAM only; if LingBot-VA is added, use its official VAE/text-encoder CPU-offload inference configuration and report backward-calibration memory as a separate measurement rather than reusing the reported inference-memory figure.\n2. Build an episode-level calibration manifest from existing RoboTwin 2.0 and LIBERO simulator episodes. Set N_cal=32 as the default to match the fixed-trajectory scale reported for QuantWAMs, with a pre-registered 16/32/64 episode sensitivity check; preserve observation histories, instructions, simulator states, action chunks, denoising seeds xi_j, simulator seeds eta_j, and native contact/task-transition flags. Output D_cal and a held-out episode/task split without mixing adjacent frames across splits.\n3. Enumerate the intervention registry R from the public WAM implementation. Each r=(branch, module, denoising_step, axis) identifies one actual quantization hook in the coupled video/action denoiser, with axis in {weight, activation}; exclude VAE-only, text-only, latent/action tokenizer, and planner-only sites. Output a deterministic registry with a lexicographic tie-break order and a mapping from each site to its kernel and bit setting.\n4. Measure single-site model interventions with matched stochastic state. For every r and calibration item j, restore the